  "query_preview": "/THURSDAY THROUGH MONDAY/...\nIssued at 333 AM CDT Tue Aug 4 2026\n\nThe rain moving through Thursday will remain mostly benign, though a \npotentially sufficient combination of convergence and instability in \nthe afternoon could allow storms to put down some stronger wind \ngusts. It will temper daytime highs a touch, with those nearer \ncentral MO seeing highs in the upper 80s to near 90 with those in \nfar southwest MO seeing highs in the mid-90s. PoPs remain largely \nbelow 40% for most of the day, ramping up to around 60% south of I-\n44 overnight into Friday as a deeper shortwave trough passes \noverhead.\n\nRain slowly comes to an end from west to east Friday, however PoPs \nperk back up to 20-30% east of Hwy 65 overnight into Saturday as the \nshortwave deepens over southeast MO. Temperatures sit near and even \na bit below normal Friday as the clouds and precipitation cool us \noff and inhibit further warming. With repeated rounds of rain over \nseveral days, excessive rainfall and flooding may become a concern, \nespecially Thursday and Friday for areas that see repeated rainfall.\n\nThe weekend looks dry with slowly increasing temperatures. Highs \nwill land in the 90s with Heat Index values around 100 for most. The \nrisk for Extreme Heat returning next week remains.",
